# Grok 5 — findings by GLM 5.3 Flash

- Source: xAI / SpaceXAI (`grok-5`, unreleased)
- Date: 2026-10-10 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> SELF-EXCLUSION (per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md` / `tasks/research.md` Rule 9):
> zero verified public benchmark numbers exist for this exact model — Grok 5
> has not shipped. This file is saved as `.md.excluded` with notes only; no
> scores are claimed and none of the figures below are averages or estimates
> dressed as scores.

## Model card

- **Name:** Grok 5
- **Short description:** xAI's (SpaceXAI since the February 2026 SpaceX acquisition) next flagship LLM, in training on the Colossus 2 supercluster and positioned by Elon Musk as the company's AGI candidate. It has never shipped and has no public results.
- **Provider / access:** none available — not listed in xAI's model docs (`docs.x.ai/docs/models`, fetched 2026-10-10), which top out at `grok-4.7`; no OpenCode Zen route (`opencode/grok-5` in this dataset is a curated placeholder, absent from the live Zen model roster). No model card or system card exists.
- **Release / knowledge:** not released as of 2026-10-10. Late-2025, Q1 2026 and Q2 2026 targets all passed with no launch; xAI shipped Grok 4.5 (2026-07-08), Grok 4.6 (2026-08-12) and Grok 4.7 (2026-09-21) instead, and Musk's 2026-09-14 roadmap places Grok 4.8 and 4.9 ahead of Grok 5.
- **IDs:** `grok-5` exists as a name only — no public API ID, no Free ID on Zen.
- **Context window:** no official number. ~1.5M tokens circulates as an estimate (unofficial); the shipping Grok 4.7 is 500K, Grok 4.3 was 1M.
- **Modalities:** expected text + image (+ likely video/audio later), consistent with Grok's direction, but nothing is specified for Grok 5 — not verified.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-10):** unannounced; any specific figure is projection. Reference points: Grok 4.7 API $2/$6 per 1M (2x above 200K prompts).
- **Architecture:** rumored 6T–10T total parameters, Mixture-of-Experts, trained on Colossus 2 (1 GW, Memphis). The only *confirmed* fact is xAI's one-line January 2026 funding announcement that the model exists and is in training; every parameter figure is disputed reporting (xAI trains several models at different sizes in parallel).

